   Flight Model: airline, from, to, departure, arrival, price, flight ID.
   Booking Model: user ID, flight ID, passenger info, booking date, reference.
   User Model: add isAdmin boolean for admin users.
2. Backend API Endpoints
   Flights
   POST /api/flights — Add flight (admin only)
   GET /api/flights — List flights
   PUT /api/flights/:id — Edit flight (admin only)
   DELETE /api/flights/:id — Delete flight (admin only)
   Bookings
   POST /api/bookings — Create booking
   GET /api/bookings — List all bookings (admin only)
   GET /api/bookings/:userId — List user’s bookings
   Users
   GET /api/users — List users (admin only)
   DELETE /api/users/:id — Delete user (admin only)
   Auth
   POST /api/login — User/admin login
   POST /api/register — User registration
